      "message": "I have noticed that on our instance and described the issue just a few minutes before this patch was proposed https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T441113\n\nWe have a single key `ssh_host_ed25519_key` which is provisioned by in our config management system (Puppet).  When running init I noticed:\n```\nGenerating SSH host key ... rsa... ecdsa 256... ecdsa 384... ecdsa 521... done\nInitialized /srv/gerrit/site_path/review_site\n```\n\nWhich led to the generation of a few extra \"rogue\" keys:\n\nssh_host_rsa_key\nssh_host_ecdsa_key\nssh_host_ecdsa_384_key\nssh_host_ecdsa_521_key\n\nI would very welcome the ability to turn that behavior off.  And maybe that can target the stable versions?",
